# Flake-window laps for 2/net/mesh/mpath on g2d (test31 test32), run from the
# main tree on the module the release chain will build (the chain's clean build
# must report the srcversion these laps ran, or they count for nothing).
#
# Window indexes of the newest genuine FAIL (11-run window, tools/criteria.py),
# read 2026-10-20 16:05Z:
#   fence_during_write  k=0 (15:27Z, D-ALLOC-WITNESS-PEER-MKDIR-ESTALE-ON-
#                       POISONED-CACHED-DIR-4CAW): 11 more runs
#   fio_perf_vs_xfs     k=1 (14:24Z): 10 more runs
#   alloc_witness       k=2 (10:44Z): 9 more runs
#   chk_clean           k=2 (10:45Z): 9 more runs
# These 10 laps and the chain's board cover all four.  fio_perf runs before
# fio_perf_vs_xfs, which grades it against the native-XFS yardstick.
#
# Bound per lap: prep_cluster 300 s + fence_during_write 60 s + fio_perf 120 s
# + fio_perf_vs_xfs 10 s + alloc_witness 120 s + chk_clean 180 s
# (tests/suite/manifest) + the chain's overhead outside the rows, measured
# about 60 s = 850 s.
850 tests/board_4node_chain.sh wm1_r131 2/net/mesh/mpath:fence_during_write,fio_perf,fio_perf_vs_xfs,alloc_witness,chk_clean@g2d
850 tests/board_4node_chain.sh wm2_r131 2/net/mesh/mpath:fence_during_write,fio_perf,fio_perf_vs_xfs,alloc_witness,chk_clean@g2d
